      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1913-03-15_WidnesExaminer_art0003" n="art0003">
        <p>BE. PATRICK'S DAV CELEBRATION.</p>
        <p>WARRINGTON WESLEYAN METHODIST</p>
        <p>CIRCUIT.</p>
        <p>4RAND "OLD ENGLISH" BAZAAR,</p>
        <p>PA RR HALL.</p>
        <p>ORIL 29TD, 30TH, MAY IsT a; 2ND, 1913.</p>
        <p>PULL PARTICULARS LATER.</p>
        <p>LANCASHIRE COUNTY ASYLUM, WINWICK, WARRINGTON. The COMMITTEE OF VISITORS INVITE TENDERS for the supply of FURNITURE, BED- STEADS, MATTRESSES, .tc„ for the Boys' Block and the Nurses' Home at the above Asylum. Tenders must be made upon forms which can be obtained from the undersigned, and must he delivered at the Asylum not later than 9 a.m. on Monday, the 7th April. The above are all to he made exactly to our samples, which can be seen at the Asylum on the dates and at the time mentioned on the Tender forms. The-Committee do not bind themselves to accept the lowest or any tender, and reserve the right to ac3ept or reject the whole or pnrt of any tender. By Order. P. IRVING DUTTON, Clerk and Steward.</p>
        <p>12th March, 1913.</p>
        <p>THE RURAL DISTRICT COUNCIL OF RUNCORN. PRIVATE STREET WORKS ACT, 1892. NOTICE IS HEREBY GIVEN, that the Rural District Council of Runoorn, being the Sanitary Authority for the Rural District of Runcorn, in the County of Chester, have, in pursuance of the Private Street Works Act, 1892, at a meeting held on the twenty-fifth day of Feuruary, 1913, by resolution, approved of certain specifications, plans and sections, estimates and provisional apportionments, prepared by their Surveyors in respect of the following streets or parts of streets : ALBERT ROAD,VICTORIA AVENUE, YORK DRIVE., In the Parish of Grappenball in the said District, and that such resolution is in the following terms that is to say :—(1) That the Rural District Council of Runcorn being the Sanitary Authority for the Rural District of Runcorn, level, pave, metal,tiag,cbannel, and make good the following streets or parts of streets in the Parish of Grappenhall, in the said District, winder the provisions of the Private Street Works Act, 1892, viz, : ALBERT ROAD,VICTORI AVENUE,YORK DRIVE. (2) That the Spocifications, Plans, Sections Estimates and Provisional Apportionments prepared and submitted by the Surveyors (Messrs Wright and Hamlyn), i respect of the said Streets be and are hereby approved. (3) That. it he, and is, hereby ordered and declared that the expenses incurred in executing the aforesaid Private Street Works shall be payable by equal annual instalments extending over a period of seven years, with interest at the rate of £4 per centum per annum. (4) That application be made to the Local Govern- ment Board for their sanction to a loan for the required amount. And NoLice is hereby further given that the approved Specifications, Plans and Sections, Estimates and Provisional Apportionments (or copies thereof certified by the Surveyors) will be kept deposited at 71, High. street, Runcorn, the Office of the Rural District Council of Runcorn and will be open to inspection at all reasonable times for a period of one month from the 15th day of March. 1913, during which period any owner of premises affected may in pursuance of Section 7 of the said Act, by written notice served on the said Council, object to the proposals of the said Council on 1 any of the grounds in such Section specified, Dated this 14th day of March, 1913. GEO. F. ASHTON, Clerk to the Rural District Counoil of Runcorn.</p>
        <p>e L''" TO £5,00 LENT DAILY Xidtl ON THESE TEI for agreed period :- 25 loan, Repay £5 10s. £25 loan, Repay £27 10s. £lO „ „ £ll 1 £3O „ „ £33 £l5 „ „ £l6 10s. I £5O „ • „ £55 £2O „ „ £22 I £lOO ~, „ £llO No sureties, no delay, no publicity. Special attention applicants from this district.</p>
        <p>RAIB</p>
        <p>CHARLES 219,BRUNSWICK ST.,OXFORD RD., MANCHESTER; and at 19, WITTON ST.. (oTet Bradley's Clothing Shop) NORTHWICH.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1913-03-15_WidnesExaminer_art0004" n="art0004">
        <head>F. HALLETT,</head>
