      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1913-03-15_WidnesExaminer_art0055" n="art0055">
        <head>°MACH TROUBLES DUE TO ACIDITY.</head>
        <p>°MACH TROUBLES DUE TO ACIDITY.</p>
        <p>8° SAYS EMINENT SPECIALIST.</p>
        <p>Ivind called stomach troubles, such as indigestion, l.lst 1 a'a atnnaach-ache and inability to retain food, are °f indicating that the stomach is out of order, fel! .- nian eases out of ten simply evidence that wind d til-nlentation is taking place in the food contents of , wae",,_,E? sto 1.. ' causing the formation of gas and acids. distens 'radethe the stomach, and causes that full, oPPressive feeling sometimes known as heartburn, an "id irritates and inflames the delicate fault 'fling of the stomach. The stomach, however, is not In at ril fer • ' .he trouble lies entirely in the entlng fond , Such fermentation is unnatural, ID: acid formation is not only unnatural, clu epra.aY:r involve the most serious conse- f en— if not prevented. To prevent or stop errnentation of the food contents of the stomach and lenaneutralise the acid, and render it bland And harm- abill half a teaspoonful of bisurated magnesia, prob- e tak b " 9 the best and most effective antacid known, should itlinil;.',4 in a quarter of a glass of hot or cold water je feiately after eating, or whenever wind or acidity _ . acidity in a This stops the fermentation, and neutralises !nroeeurr.tted few moments. Fermentation, wind iv acidity are dangerous and unnecessary. Stop or 49'. ent them by the use of a proper antacid, such as magnesia, -which can be obtained from any 4 Mist, and thus enable the stomach to do its work Pro.,,r, . da V 'Yr without being hindered by poisonous gas and ngerous acid B.-14. p.p.</p>
        <p>ALL SAINTS CHURCH. Mr C 11' tt45.6 o ingwood performed the ceremony of cutting _ __ 1. rat sod for the new church to be erected in urow ..,ttle, Earlestown , on Saturday afternoon. Votes of ,114,11114 were afterwards accorded Mr Collingwood, and 10collection realized .£54 ss, a cheque for ,£5O being igluded. On Saturday night the members of the Girls' Qtluib' together with the members of the Physical .t_ tura 4 Society, gave ft capital concert to a good ate:ll- '1 ttt "Jolt's Assembly Room.</p>
