        <p>LANCA6IIIIIE COUNTY ASY LUM WIN WICK WARRINGTON. The Committee of Visitors invite TENDERS for PAINTING part of the outside wood and iron work at the Asylum. Persons desirous of tendering must measure up the work themselves between 10 a.m. and 12 noon, or 2 p.m, and 5 n.in. on any of the following days, viz :—March 25th, 26th. and 27th only, and must be at the steward's Office at either 10 a.m. or 2 p.m. on one of those days. Tenders must be made on forms which can be obtained from the undersigne4, and must be delivered at the Asylum not later than 9 am. on the 7th April, I addressed to the Chairman, and endorsed "Tender for Painting." The Committee do not bind themselves to accept the lowest or any tender.—By order. P. IRVING DUTTON. 12th March, 1912, Clerk &amp; Steward.</p>
