        <p>NVARRINGTON BLUE COAT CHARITY SCHOOL. NOTICE IS HEREBY GIVN4N, that tbe Trustees of theabove SCHOOL will, at their next QuHrterly Meet- ing, on the 21st day of April itext, proceed to elect two Children (1 Boy and 1 Girl) to Vacancies now existing in the Institution. No Candidate will be eligible unless an application on his or her behalf (forms of which may he obtained from the Clerk, at his Cffice, 3, NVinwick Street), shall have been made to the Clerk to the Trustees, at least fourteen days previous to till day of Meeting. In elecing Children, the Trustees make Orphans their first choice. Ttiose deprived of one parent come next in consideration, and after them the children of parents who have the greatest number and the slenderest means. Dated th:s 15th day of March. 1913, HENRY GREENALL, Clerk to the Trustees.</p>
