        <p>A PAR nr OF CONSCRIPTION. Mr Francis Neilson, member for Hide Divisior.s speaking at Hollingworth, near Hyde, on Saturday evening said he believed the Conservative psrty was becoming more and more a party of conscription. Lord Roberts and those with him really meant ccnscription- The truth had leaked out at last that the militarist. wanted to he prepared with a large army so that they could send it to the support of France. Great Britain had had too 'much of fighting other people's battles, and had enough to do at home to fight her own without worrying about anyone else. The people were drawn into the South African War, which cost them £250,000,000, besides the many lives lost, and after the war was over the result never brought them back a penny, • MASONIC NURSING HOME. It is proposed to secure a building situated in a con- venient position in London for use as a Masonic Nursing Home. There will be accommodation for between 30 and 40 patients.</p>
