        <p>Pardoe having no chance, Latchford were now having the best of matters, and a brilliant effort by Jackson from the left deserved a better fate than to be just put over the bar. Barnton defended well. No further score took place before the interval, when the score wr a:— Latchford, one goal ; Barnton Villa, nil. Resuming, the Villa asserted themselves, Lei caster receiving a nice piss from Latham, git away ami centred nicely to Sharp, for the latter to give Simcock a terr:fic shot, which he safely cleared. Sin:cock again was in evidence with a smart clearance from Loos. Barnton still kept up the pia ssure, Leicester again got away and placing nicely in the centre, enabled Lees to equalize the scores. Latchford now suffered a severe loss, Robinson having to leave the field. With their opponents' defence weakened, Barnton had most of the game. Simcock gathered a shot from Leices,er, lost possession of the ball, Sharps having uo difficulty in giving them the lead. Lees added a third goal but although to all intents beaten, Latchford struggled on and a timely pass by Webb to Shakeshaft wive the latter a chance. From his shot one of the backs handled, and Taylor with a capital drive from the consequent penalty gave Pardoe no chance. This was just the tonic required for Latchford and they fought strenuously to get on level terms. The Barnton defence, however, held out,and taking the gam on the whole deserved their victory with the scores : Barnton Villa, three goals : Lltchforl, two gills. WIDNES AND DISTRICT ALLIANCE. GREAT SANKEY V. BALFOUR ROAD OLD BOYS.— Runcorn to-day. Great Sankey Team :—J Bond, goal ; E Glover, sere, B J Kelly, full backs ; E Glover, jun., It' Millington ,H I'a3ne, half backs ; E Darlington, T Whitfield, T Cook (capt), A Grainger, W Booth, forwards.</p>
