        <p>Latchford Baptist Boys' Brigade. The quarterly church parade was held on Sunday evening last, the speaker being Major S A Morgan, Commandant of the Boys' Life Brigade, Manchester Battalion. The boys, bedded by the bugle band,marched to the chapel, where they were inspected by Major Morgan, who highly complimented the officers and members on their smartness and efficiency, which he said was remarkable in view of the shortness of their history, extending as it did over little more than twelve months. At the service the chaplain, Rev J S Chedburn, presided, and Major Morgan delivered a stirring and powerful address, his subject being "The call of Christ to the first disciples."</p>
